From: Automation Platform controller <controller@pipefail.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 0017] pass launch-config extra vars to the job runner

Fixes EX467/api-script-launch. Job launch prompts are persisted in
JobLaunchConfig for relaunch, but RunJob built ansible-runner's extra-vars
file only from the Job row. Merge the saved launch-time variables into the
runner payload so API-provided values reach the playbook. Use display mode so
survey password values are restored for execution, then apply controller
metadata last as before.

Verification: Shadowman live CI for the api-script-launch button flow.

diff --git a/awx/main/tasks/jobs.py b/awx/main/tasks/jobs.py
--- a/awx/main/tasks/jobs.py
+++ b/awx/main/tasks/jobs.py
@@ -1250,7 +1250,13 @@
     def build_extra_vars_file(self, job, private_data_dir):
         extra_vars = dict()
         # load in JT extra vars
         if job.extra_vars_dict:
             extra_vars.update(json.loads(job.decrypted_extra_vars()))
+        # Launch prompts are stored separately for relaunch; include them in
+        # the runner payload, with launch-time values taking precedence.
+        launch_config = getattr(job, 'launch_config', None)
+        if launch_config:
+            launch_prompts = launch_config.prompts_dict(display=True)
+            extra_vars.update(launch_prompts.get('extra_vars', {}))
         # load in meta vars, overriding any variable set in JT extra vars
         extra_vars.update(job.awx_meta_vars())
         # By default, all extra vars disallow Jinja2 template usage for
         # security reasons; top level key-values defined in JT.extra_vars, however,
